<!--
  Splunk_in_KB-output.drawio — machine conversion of tests/fixtures/Splunk_in_KB.png
  Produced 2026-08-10 on the Spark by Qwen3-VL-30B-A3B-Instruct-NVFP4 (slot 0), with the
  production ragfarm-vision system prompt.

  HOW — two passes, because one pass cannot do this.
    pass 1  boxes only, edges explicitly forbidden  -> 98 cells,  8,847 tok, finish=stop
    pass 2  edges only, given pass 1's box ids      -> 26 edges,  1,750 tok, finish=stop
    merge   pass 2's <mxCell edge> block inserted before </root>. Mechanical, nothing else.

  WHY TWO. Asked for the whole diagram at once the same model runs its entire 24,576-token
  budget dry inside an edge repetition loop: 24 boxes, then 312 edges for a source that has
  ~26, 116 of them at one node. Forbidding edges in pass 1 removes the loop completely, and
  pass 2 — given a fixed list of ids to connect — emits 26 unique edges and stops.
  Raw numbers: docs/measurements/2026-08-09-instruct-vs-thinking-drawio.json

  FIDELITY against the PNG: 28 entities as swimlanes with their attribute rows, the PoC
  container, the Legenda frame, colours by domain, 26 edges. Known gaps: a few boxes are
  ~20px too short so the last attribute row clips, the four legend boxes sit beside the
  Legenda frame rather than inside it, and the Tribe/Squad/Person column is green where the
  original is grey. No ER endpoint markers (crow's foot / zero-one).
-->
